      "writtenOn": "2021-01-04T16:24:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So what happens if someone boots a TWRP with this feature, changes the folder name, and then boots into a TWRP that doesn\u0027t have it? There would be two folders, and the settings file would be gone. And then if booting back into the TWRP with this feature, which settings would be used, since both would exist? Is there any handling for that situation?",
      "revId": "999d1059562d9fc6fbe8ea2f46698663936b1d71",
      "serverId": "9c1c7d72-6534-4d44-b0ea-39f63e804833"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "852fda83_0fcd2cfa",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 606
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-04T21:16:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let me tell one thing is that by this commit, Rec will not save any constant location of the TWRP folder.\nIf its able to find .\u003chashedName\u003e, then rec will select that folder as TWRP folder and if its not able to find that file then it will look for .twrps. Once it founds .twrps, rec will renamed that from .twrps to .\u003chashedName\u003e\n\n\nNow if user boots into old version of TWRP, Old version will create TWRP folder with .twrps file.\n\nNow if user go back to new version of twrp, It will look for .\u003chashedName\u003e as I said above. Note that - It will not delete the old TWRP folder (Because I thought \n its unsafe). But it will not use that folder if any folder available with .\u003chashedName\u003e",
      "parentUuid": "d03ef037_2dbaddd2",
      "revId": "999d1059562d9fc6fbe8ea2f46698663936b1d71",
      "serverId": "9c1c7d72-6534-4d44-b0ea-39f63e804833"
    },
    {
